@startuml
title RuleSphere - Shadow and Canary Rollout\nUC-15..17
autonumber
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #177E8D
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBackgroundColor #EAF6F8

actor "Release Manager" as Manager
actor "Consumer Application" as Client
boundary "Management API" as API
participant AuthorizationService as Auth
participant Deployment
participant DistributionService as Distribution
participant "Runtime / RolloutPolicy" as Runtime
participant "Production GraphExecutor" as Production
participant "Shadow GraphExecutor" as Shadow
database "Protected ShadowComparison" as Diffs

' Phase 1: Configure Rollout
Manager -> API: Configure Shadow and/or Canary(candidate, policy)
activate API

API -> Auth: authorize(manager, rollout, scope)
activate Auth
Auth --> API: Access decision
deactivate Auth

break Unauthorized
  API --> Manager: Access denied
end

API -> Deployment: Check approved artifact and rollout eligibility
activate Deployment

break Candidate ineligible
  Deployment --> API: Reject rollout
  API --> Manager: Policy error
end

Deployment -> Distribution: Distribute artifact and rollout configuration
activate Distribution

ref over Distribution,Runtime
  Load and validate before serving; see diagram 05
end ref

Distribution --> Deployment: Configuration publication status
deactivate Distribution

Deployment --> API: Rollout configured
deactivate Deployment

API --> Manager: Rollout status
deactivate API

' Phase 2: Production Request with Canary Routing
Client -> Runtime: Unpinned evaluation(input, subjectKey, claims)
activate Runtime

ref over Client,Runtime
  Authorize scope and resolve eligible snapshot; see diagram 06
end ref

Runtime -> Runtime: Apply sticky percentage / configured cohort policy
note right of Runtime
  Fixed rollout configuration + same subject key
  must produce the same cohort assignment.
  Hash algorithm and cohort precedence require ADR.
end note

alt Selected for Canary
  Runtime -> Production: Execute eligible loaded candidate snapshot
  activate Production
  Production --> Runtime: Candidate outcome + execution ID
  deactivate Production
else Selected for Active
  Runtime -> Production: Execute loaded Active snapshot
  activate Production
  Production --> Runtime: Active outcome + execution ID
  deactivate Production
end

Runtime --> Client: Production response
deactivate Runtime

' Phase 3: Asynchronous Shadow Processing
opt Shadow enabled for mirrored input
  opt Production request used Canary
    Runtime -> Production: Evaluate fixed Active baseline on mirrored input
    activate Production
    Production --> Runtime: Active baseline outcome (comparison only)
    deactivate Production
  end
  Runtime ->> Shadow: Execute approved Shadow snapshot with mirrored input
  activate Shadow
  Shadow -> Shadow: Evaluate independently
  Runtime ->> Diffs: Supply correlated protected Active baseline outcome
  Shadow ->> Diffs: Capture protected Active/Shadow outcome comparison
  deactivate Shadow
  note over Runtime,Diffs
    Shadow never alters the production response.
    With Canary coexistence, compare to Active; evaluate an
    Active baseline separately when production used Canary.
    Scheduling and comparison correlation are design decisions.
  end note
end

' Phase 4: Query Diff Analysis
Manager -> API: Query Shadow differences
activate API

API -> Auth: authorize(manager, view differences, scope)
activate Auth
Auth --> API: Access decision
deactivate Auth

alt Authorized
  API -> Diffs: Read scoped protected comparisons
  activate Diffs
  Diffs --> API: Outcome differences
  deactivate Diffs
  API --> Manager: Diff analysis
else Unauthorized
  API --> Manager: Access denied
end
deactivate API

@enduml
